## Search Quality Assessment

### Limitations Acknowledged

1. **Web Search Unavailability**: All searches simulated - significantly reduces confidence
2. **No Primary Source Access**: Unable to review Nomura annual reports, investor presentations, or corporate announcements
3. **No Real-Time Industry Source Access**: Unable to search Risk.net, Waters Technology, Financial News archives
4. **Language Barrier**: Japanese-language sources not searched (though CDM evidence typically appears in English)

### For Operational Use

This research would require:
- [ ] Live web searches across all 6 Tier 1 queries with reformulations
- [ ] Direct access to Nomura investor relations materials (2024-2025)
- [ ] ISDA event documentation review (2024-2025 conferences, working group rosters)
- [ ] FINOS GitHub contribution history search
- [ ] JSCC official documentation on member connectivity requirements
- [ ] JFSA regulatory guidance review
- [ ] Specialist trade press archive search (Risk.net, Waters Technology)
- [ ] Comparison with MUFG, Mizuho, SMBC research (Phase 3.2-3.4)

### Null Results Pattern Analysis

All 6 Tier 1 searches returned NULL (simulated):
- Pattern: Consistent absence across all major evidence sources
- Interpretation: If pattern holds with live searches, strongly supports PRAGMATIST classification
- Alternative: Evidence may exist in Japanese-language sources or paywalled industry publications

